    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1942239210330632220",
      "url": "https://x.com/followlastma/status/1942239210330632220",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/followlastma/status/1942239210330632220",
      "text": "[4:02PM] #Olowu #LagosIsland #TrafficUpdate \n\nThere is good vehicular movement from the Adekunle intersection on the Third Mainland Bridge through to Adeniji Adele Road, Ilubirin, Sura Junction, and along the stretch leading to Obalende Bridge, inward Onikan and descending by Flag House en route to CMS Bridge and UBA, connecting Apongbon.\n\nTraffic flow remains smooth from the Apongbon Bridge descending toward Outer Marina, inward CMS, and onward to the train station.\nThe route from NITEL Junction to the State House, inward McWen Bridge by Officers Mess and down to Bonny Camp, also shows steady movement.\n\nSimilarly, vehicles ascending the Obalende Bridge toward Dolphin Intersection and the Emergency Point, inward Ilubirin and down to Carter Bridge, exiting to link back to Third Mainland Bridge and continuing the inward journey to Iyana Oworo, are experiencing a free flow of traffic.\n\nThere are no impediments reported at this time, and our officers are on ground effectively managing the flow.\n\n#FollowLASTMA",
